From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CoreRouter <noreply@corerouter>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 00:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] ospfd: log a full router-LSA once, not once per link

A router-LSA holds at most ~5330 links: the stream is grown once, to
OSPF_MAX_PACKET_SIZE - OSPF_MAX_LSA_SIZE bytes. Past that, link_info_set()
logs "Out of space in LSA stream" for every link left out, again on every
new instance. With 10000 interfaces in one area, ospfd logged 21.8
million such lines (2.5 GB) in about two minutes while they were being
configured, and filled the disk of a small router.

Count the links left out instead, and log once when the router-LSA of an
area becomes full (how many links it has and how many did not fit) and
once when all of them fit again.
---
 ospfd/ospf_lsa.c | 26 +++++++++++++++++++++-----
 ospfd/ospfd.h    |  3 +++
 2 files changed, 24 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/ospfd/ospf_lsa.c b/ospfd/ospf_lsa.c
index baf11d3ff6..b7d91601ee 100644
--- a/ospfd/ospf_lsa.c
+++ b/ospfd/ospf_lsa.c
@@ -460,6 +460,12 @@ static uint16_t ospf_link_cost(struct ospf_interface *oi)
 		return OSPF_OUTPUT_COST_INFINITE;
 }
 
+/*
+ * Links that did not fit in the router-LSA being built: counted here and
+ * logged once per area by ospf_router_lsa_body_set(), not once per link.
+ */
+static unsigned int router_lsa_links_left_out;
+
 /* Set a link information. */
 char link_info_set(struct stream **s, struct in_addr id, struct in_addr data,
 		   uint8_t type, uint8_t tos, uint16_t cost)
@@ -490,11 +496,7 @@ char link_info_set(struct stream **s, struct in_addr id, struct in_addr data,
 		}
 
 		if (ret == OSPF_MAX_LSA_SIZE) {
-			flog_warn(
-				EC_OSPF_LSA_SIZE,
-				"%s: Out of space in LSA stream, left %zd, size %zd",
-				__func__, STREAM_WRITEABLE(*s),
-				STREAM_SIZE(*s));
+			router_lsa_links_left_out++;
 			return 0;
 		}
 	}
@@ -791,8 +793,22 @@ void ospf_router_lsa_body_set(struct stream **s, struct ospf_area *area)
 	stream_putw(*s, 0);
 
 	/* Set all link information. */
+	router_lsa_links_left_out = 0;
 	cnt = router_lsa_link_set(s, area);
 
+	/*
+	 * Out of space: say it when it starts and when it ends, not for each
+	 * link of each new instance (with thousands of interfaces in one
+	 * area that is millions of lines).
+	 */
+	if (router_lsa_links_left_out && !area->router_lsa_links_left_out)
+		flog_warn(EC_OSPF_LSA_SIZE,
+			  "Area %pI4: router-LSA is full with %u links, %u more left out",
+			  &area->area_id, cnt, router_lsa_links_left_out);
+	else if (!router_lsa_links_left_out && area->router_lsa_links_left_out)
+		zlog_info("Area %pI4: router-LSA fits all its %u links again", &area->area_id, cnt);
+	area->router_lsa_links_left_out = router_lsa_links_left_out;
+
 	/* Set # of links here. */
 	stream_putw_at(*s, putp, cnt);
 }
diff --git a/ospfd/ospfd.h b/ospfd/ospfd.h
index 0b0ffd3b85..3ff3c0af64 100644
--- a/ospfd/ospfd.h
+++ b/ospfd/ospfd.h
@@ -518,6 +518,9 @@ struct ospf_area {
 	int lsa_pos_count; /* links in the router-LSA last built */
 	int lsa_pos_size;  /* allocated entries */
 
+	/* Links that did not fit in the router-LSA last built. */
+	unsigned int router_lsa_links_left_out;
+
 	/* Area ID. */
 	struct in_addr area_id;
 
